I don't know why things have changed at your site, but you might to
consider  the following things:

1) The flow control parameters in your stty settings (see the unix
man page 
   for stty - look for ixon, ixoff, ixany). With software flow
control 
   disabled, terminfo enforces "mandatory" padding, which affects the
"delay" 
   routines used in the throwing and "resistance-special-effects"
code. I've 
   seen very broken behavior of the kind you describe with my
terminal's flow 
   control disabled (on a 3B2/600 running SysVr3.2.1). Actually, I
threw one 
   object, and the display hadn't finished, even 5 minutes later!
Depending
   on your computer, you may not have the option of what kind of flow
control
   to use... 

2) Setting the "nonulls" option might fix this. The effect of this
option is
   that nethack will think that your terminal has no null characters
(which
   is what terminfo uses for padding), and it will use an alternate
method of 
   generating the delays. 

3) Maybe your game administrators moved to terminfo from termcap in
their
   attempts to get color. If so, it might be necessary to roll that
change
   back until this terminal stuff gets sorted out.

I post this article (rather than replying via mail) because it is
likely that others might run into these problems.
